{"task":"Refuse key material and secrets from a site root","goals":"Close a reported leak in which a site's private key was downloadable from its own web root","status":"Waiting","recorded_at":"2026-09-10T04:03:01Z","body":"Reported by the matsu port session and reproduced here before changing anything: against the\nreal rendered config, GET /seasonal-drops.ldev+2-key.pem returned 200, 1704 bytes, beginning\n-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----.\n\nA site root is served whole. `file_server` has no notion of a file being private, and the\nserver runs as root, so mode 0600 stops nothing. Both templates had a bare `file_server` and\nno matcher of any kind — nine of them across the wildcard file alone.\n\nThe only other thing in the way is the loopback `bind`, and that line is documented, in the\ntemplate, as the one to delete for testing from a phone. So the invitation the comment makes\nand the exposure it creates are one line apart: delete it and every certificate and .env\nunder the sites directory is on the network.\n\nBoth templates now refuse those paths before any handler sees them, with 404 rather than 403\n— a refusal confirms the file is there, and for somebody scanning, knowing a key file exists\nis most of what they wanted.\n\nTwo things this does NOT do, both worth stating rather than implying:\n\nIt is a floor, not a licence to keep secrets in a web root. The matcher lists the names that\nturn up: .pem .key .crt .p12 .pfx .jks, .env and its variants, .git, .ssh, .htpasswd. It\ncannot cover every name a secret might have, which is why doctor now names the files it finds\nrather than reporting the matcher as sufficient.\n\nAnd it cannot reach a standalone site's own Caddyfile. That file is the owner's and `ldev\napply` never rewrites it, so a site created before this still serves its own directory\nunguarded — seasonal-drops.ldev on this machine is exactly that. doctor reports both\nseparately: key material in a served directory, and an own Caddyfile predating the refusal.\n\nVerified by serving each template on a spare port, unprivileged, against a directory holding\na fake key, a fake certificate and a .env: all three 404, index.html and / still 200. Both\ntemplates, because fixing only the wildcard would have moved the leak rather than closed it —\nseasonal-drops is served by its own Caddyfile, not the wildcard, which is also why the first\nattempt at reproducing this through `ldev render` measured the wrong path.\n\ntest/secrets.test.sh runs that as a test rather than asserting on config text, since the\nquestion is what the server does, not what the file says.\n","parent_commit":"3f97668e596025919154842949e0e67e0360f5a4","repo":"brave-cedar-fb33","pct":"60","tasks":[{"id":"repro","content":"Reproduce the reported leak against the real config before changing anything","status":"completed"},{"id":"wildcard","content":"@forbidden matcher in the wildcard template, both the TLS and .localhost blocks","status":"completed"},{"id":"site","content":"Same refusal in the standalone-site template, since seasonal-drops is served by its own Caddyfile","status":"completed"},{"id":"doctor","content":"doctor names key material in a served directory, and own Caddyfiles predating the refusal","status":"completed"},{"id":"tests","content":"test/secrets.test.sh — both templates served on a spare port, refusal measured not asserted from text","status":"completed","created_at":"2026-09-10T01:14:35.832Z","status_at":"2026-09-10T01:14:35.832Z"},{"id":"docs","content":"README troubleshooting row and tests listing","status":"completed"},{"id":"seasonal-certs","content":"Move the four .pem files out of ~/Sites/seasonal-drops.ldev, and guard its own Caddyfile","status":"pending","human_reason":"Two private keys and two certificates sit in that site root. The wildcard server refuses those paths now, but seasonal-drops is served by its OWN Caddyfile, which ldev apply never rewrites — so it stays unguarded until either the matcher is pasted in or the files move. Moving someone's certificates is not something to do unasked; the matsu session moved its own to ~/.config/matsu-dev-certs/ and left these alone for the same reason."},{"id":"merge-branches","content":"Merge claude/lucid-ember-7451 — it needs 917b259, and master needs its TUI and mkcert signing","status":"pending","human_reason":"The two branches are complementary: that branch merged master at acf343b and kept its logic. It lacks only 917b259 (ldev update); master lacks its TUI (lib/tui.sh, test/tui-menu.test.sh, --plain) and its mkcert signing. The two incompatibilities are fixed on this branch, so the merge should be mechanical — but landing another session's branch is Bryce's call, and that session may still be working in it.","created_at":"2026-09-10T03:56:49.653Z","status_at":"2026-09-10T03:56:49.653Z"},{"id":"triaj-swap","content":"Retire sh.brew.caddy so ldev can own 443","status":"pending","human_reason":"Needs sudo and a terminal, which this session has neither of. The matsu session confirms matsu.ldev needs nothing beyond being a folder in ~/Sites, and triaj.ldev is now a proxy site pointing at the same 5273 the Homebrew caddy uses, so nothing is left waiting on either. Re-run install.sh; it finds sh.brew.caddy and offers to take it down.","created_at":"2026-09-10T03:09:42.808Z","status_at":"2026-09-10T03:09:42.808Z"},{"id":"rehome-run","content":"Run ldev rehome against seasonal-drops","status":"pending","human_reason":"Rewrites live site data: 16,224 database rows plus WP_HOME/WP_SITEURL in wp-config.php. The command refuses to run without a terminal to confirm on. Do it after the swap.","created_at":"2026-09-09T19:22:30.481Z","status_at":"2026-09-09T19:22:30.481Z"}],"agent":"claude-code","changelog":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","code_quality":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","vulnerabilities":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","code_style_suggestions":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","reusability":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","system_compatibility":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","sessions":[{"provider":"claude","id":"3e8f56a2-7837-42a5-adfb-4e072f3876ee","title":"https://sites.ldev/ (or any other name I put) doesn't auto redirect to the projects dashboard","linked_at":"2026-09-10T04:03:01Z"}],"review_run":{"state":"did_not_run","at":"2026-09-10T04:03:01Z","attempts":1,"reason":"Review skipped at the caller's request (--no-review / automatedReview: false)."}}
